From f6e4e0f00009e5f3628317df5222aa9e079d961e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cjybyjk <cjybyjk@zjnu.edu.cn>
Date: Mon, 20 Jan 2025 04:34:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] PixelOS: Disguise props for music apps for status bar
 lyric

Some music apps (NetEase Cloud Music, QQ Music, KuGou, Kuwo, Migu and
Honor Music) only publish the statusbar-lyric ticker notifications when
they believe they run on a supported ROM. Disguise those apps as a
Meizu device (Flyme) at Application instantiation time, enabled by
default via persist.sys.disguise_props_for_music_app (default true);
users can opt out with:
  adb shell setprop persist.sys.disguise_props_for_music_app false

Device values verified against app-side detection (2026-11, smali):
- NetEase Cloud Music 9.6.22: Build.DISPLAY.toLowerCase().startsWith
  ("flyme") || Build.BRAND.toLowerCase()=="meizu" (z3.S/z3.U), plus
  reflection of Notification.FLAG_ALWAYS_SHOW_TICKER /
  FLAG_ONLY_UPDATE_TICKER. DEVICE is not checked.
- QQ Music 20.9.8.8: same ticker flag reflection plus
  RemoteLyricController$a.d(): Build.DEVICE must NOT be "Note9" or
  "M1852" (Meizu models where QQ disables the feature) - hence
  DEVICE=m1892 (Meizu 16th Plus codename), which passes both apps.

Port of the Pixel Experience patch from linlinger ginkgo tree
(patches/framework-base/0003-base-Reset-props-for-status-bar-lyric),
hooked at both newApplication() paths, like evox cnb GamePropsSpoofService wiring.

